ead_input_tokens\": 1104, \"output_tokens\": 93}\n---\n30 logs/usage.jsonl\n"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"The log confirms the diagnosis: every `save_fact` is followed by a round with `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and ~1000 `cache_creation_input_tokens` — the whole system prompt is being re-created. The cause is visible in `build_system` (bot.py:130-133): the static `INSTRUCTIONS` and the volatile athlete context (including the facts list) are concatenated into **one** cache block, so one appended fact changes the block and evicts everything.\n\nLet me check one design constraint before fixing — Anthropic caches have a minimum prefix length, so I need to know how the static block must be sized:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_tjEZnT2gojkJCkeQriPrRvRj","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport bot, datetime\\na = bot.load_athlete(\\\"42\\\")\\ntoday = datetime.date.today()\\ninstr = bot.INSTRUCTIONS\\nctx = bot.athlete_context(a, today)\\nprint(\\\"instructions chars:\\\", len(instr), \\\"≈ tokens:\\\", len(instr)//4)\\nprint(\\\"context chars:\\\", len(ctx), \\\"≈ tokens:\\\", len(ctx)//4)\\nheader = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(l for l in ctx.splitlines() if not l.startswith(\\\"- \\\"))\\nfacts = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(l for l in ctx.splitlines() if l.startswith(\\\"- \\\"))\\nprint(\\\"header chars:\\\", len(header), \\\"≈ tokens:\\\", len(header)//4)\\nprint(\\\"facts chars:\\\", len(facts), \\\"≈ tokens:\\\", len(facts)//4)\\nEOF\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_2OE3aQhenWw7HVr5r2caJhXW","function":{"name":"WebSearch","arguments":"{\"query\":\"Anthropic prompt caching minimum cacheable prompt length 1024 tokens multiple cache_control breakpoints\"}"}}]}
